[[Supportive care]]

Topic outline: antiresorptive therapy for bone health in oncology.

!! Clinical settings
* Bone metastases and myeloma-related bone disease.
* Cancer treatment-associated bone loss and fracture risk.
* Adjuvant use in breast cancer.

!! Agents and treatment planning
* Bisphosphonates and denosumab.
* Agent selection, indication-specific dosing, and treatment intervals.
* Duration, de-escalation, and discontinuation planning.

!! Assessment and monitoring
* Dental assessment and osteonecrosis of the jaw.
* Renal function, calcium, and vitamin D status.
* Hypocalcemia, atypical fractures, and other adverse effects.

